        "acc_tradition": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "BACKED BY GENERATIONS OF HONDURAN TRADITION",
            "content": "<p>Not all Batana oils are real — most on the market are refined, diluted, or blended with cheap carrier oils.</p><p>Ours is cold-pressed from the nuts of the American oil palm (<em>Elaeis oleifera</em>) in the rainforests of La Mosquitia, Honduras, harvested by Miskito communities using methods passed down for generations. They call it the miracle oil.</p><p>It's untouched, unrefined, and naturally rich in vitamin E, omegas, and antioxidants that refined blends can't match.</p>"
          }
        },
        "acc_different": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "HOW IS THIS OIL ANY DIFFERENT?",
            "layout": "compare",
            "items": "Grown in Honduras\nDeep amber, nutrient-rich color\nNatural, earthy aroma\nMelts on contact, absorbs fast\nRich in omegas & antioxidants\nSupports edges & growth",
            "items_secondary": "Inferior, mass-produced\nPale or greenish color\nRancid or chemical smell\nLeaves greasy residue\nNutrients stripped away\nCoats hair without feeding it",
            "compare_ours_title": "PURE BATANA OIL",
            "compare_theirs_title": "FAKE BATANA OIL",
            "content": "<p><strong>The color:</strong> Real raw Batana is a deep amber-brown from natural tocotrienols. Light-colored oil has been refined.</p><p><strong>The texture:</strong> Naturally thick — it may solidify in cooler temperatures, which is a sign of purity. Warm it in your hands and it melts right back.</p><p><strong>The smell:</strong> Distinctively nutty and earthy. If it's odorless, the good stuff has been stripped out.</p><p><strong>The rule:</strong> One ingredient, nothing added. Ever.</p>"
          }
        },
        "acc_howto": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "HOW TO USE THIS OIL",
            "layout": "steps",
            "items": "Massage into scalp & edges\nLeave in 30 min or overnight\nWash out & style as usual\nRepeat 3–4 times a week",
            "content": "<p><strong>Scalp & edges:</strong> Massage a small amount into the scalp and edges 3–4 times per week. Leave in overnight (silk cap recommended) or at least 30 minutes before washing.</p><p><strong>Lengths & ends:</strong> Warm a little between your palms and work through to seal moisture and add shine.</p><p><strong>Beard & skin:</strong> Apply a thin layer after washing — a dime-sized amount goes a long way.</p><p><strong>Storage:</strong> Keep in a cool, dry place. If it hardens, warm the jar briefly — it works exactly the same.</p>"
          }
        },
        "acc_ingredients": {
          "type": "accordion",
          "settings": {
            "title": "INGREDIENTS",
            "layout": "icons",
            "items": "1 ingredient: 100% raw Batana oil — nothing added\nVitamin E: shields, heals & locks in moisture\nOmega 3-6-9: restores softness, bounce & shine\nVitamin A: renews scalp & strengthens strands",
            "content": "<p><strong>100% Raw Batana Oil.</strong> One single ingredient, in its purest form, straight from the Honduran rainforest. Nothing added, nothing diluted.</p><p><strong>Naturally contains:</strong> Vitamin E complex (antioxidant-rich repair that locks in moisture), Omega 3-6-9 fatty acids (restore softness, bounce, and shine), and Vitamin A / beta-carotene (supports cell turnover for a healthy scalp and resilient hair).</p>"
